K:
%%begintext

NOTE: This is a test run to see if easier versions might be useful especially for new players. 
I can't promise to do it for every SPUDS tune, but this trial run could give you ideas on how 
to make notey tunes more accessible for your skill level and instrument.
     Sarah - -  ssgowan@gmail.com

Leaders: James McPeak and Steve Epstein

Reel Sets:
1. Marie, Sauce ton Pain (G) / Pointe au Pic (C) 
2. Scollay's Reel (Em) / Maureen of Gibberland (D) 
3. Old Grey Mare (G) / Old Joe Clark (Amix) 
4. Pretty Little Dog (Ador) / Say No More (C) 
5. The Rakes of Mallow (G) / Sandy River Belles (G) 
6. Hollow Poplar (G) / Jaybird (D) 
7. Tam Lin (Dm) / Bus Stop Reel (Am) 
8. Red Prairie Dawn (A) / Frosty the Snowman (D) / The Wren (D) 
9. The Calvin Cycle (Dm) / Reign Of Love (Em) 

Jig to Reel:
10. Cottonwood (Am) / Dancing Bear (Em) 
11. Blue Jig (Am) / Where's That Blue-Eyed Lady? (Am) 

Jig Sets:
12. Lad O'Beirne's (D) / Gaspacho (G) 
13. The Doubtful Guest (Em) / Korolenko's Backyard (G) 
14. New Rigged Ship (D) / Off She Goes (D) 
15. Night They Reversed The Curse (D) / The Comeback (A) 

Waltzes:
16. Marge's Anniversary Waltz (Gm) 
17. Bonnie At Morn (Am) 

Schottische:
18. Zisook's Schottische (Dm) 

%%endtext

